From 23a1665f63bd5e50bd2b2a97a78ca7d6762ded56 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 22:50:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] settings: "HDR at more than 8 bits where the card sends RGB
 at 8 (NVIDIA)" on by default

On GeForce GTX 10 cards and the TITAN V (driver 580), which send HDR over HDMI in RGB at 8 bits at most,
the setting sends it in YCbCr 4:2:2 at 10 bits; that was seen on a GeForce GTX 1060 with an LG OLED65C8,
straight and through a Denon AVR (issue 17: "HDR10 10-bit output is working perfectly!"; the kernel log
said "goes out in YCbCr 4:2:2 at 10 bpc"). On driver 620 the same setting sends YCbCr 4:2:2 at 12 bits
where NVKMS would leave HDR in RGB at 8 bits (GeForce GTX 16, RTX 20; newer cards at 3840x2160 and 50
or 60 Hz without an HDMI 2.1 link). Both run the link at the clock of RGB at 8 bits, which the display
already shows in that mode, in a format that it declares; where it does not lock onto it, the mode goes
back to RGB at 8 bits for the session by itself (the change before this one), so the setting is on by
default now. Turned off, or with "HDR output depth" at 8 bits, HDR goes out as before. RGB at 12 bits
(videoscreen.hadeshdrdeepcolour) stays off: it raises the link to 1.5 times the clock.

Kodi keeps a setting that equals its default as "the default" (guisettings.xml, default="true"), so it
is on after this update also where it was off before; "HDR output depth" at 8 bits, which a user may
have chosen for the way the TV handles deeper input, still holds HDR at 8 bits. Not tried on hardware
with driver 620.
---
 system/settings/settings.xml | 6 ++++--
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/system/settings/settings.xml b/system/settings/settings.xml
index 4e44533..c2a5b66 100644
--- a/system/settings/settings.xml
+++ b/system/settings/settings.xml
@@ -4087,7 +4087,9 @@
         <control type="spinner" format="string" />
       </setting>
       <!-- Hades: HDR at more than 8 bits on NVIDIA graphics where the driver would send it over HDMI in
-           RGB at 8 bits (HdrMoreBits.h): YCbCr 4:2:2 at the clock of RGB at 8 bits -->
+           RGB at 8 bits (HdrMoreBits.h): YCbCr 4:2:2 at the clock of RGB at 8 bits, on by default (seen
+           at 10 bits on a GeForce GTX 1060 with an LG OLED65C8, issue 17), where the display locks onto
+           it: a mode that it does not lock onto goes back to RGB at 8 bits for the session -->
       <setting id="videoscreen.hadeshdrmorebits" type="boolean" label="41011" help="41012">
         <requirement>
           <and>
@@ -4099,7 +4101,7 @@
           <dependency type="visible" on="property" name="supportshdrmorebits"/>
         </dependencies>
         <level>3</level>
-        <default>false</default>
+        <default>true</default>
         <control type="toggle" />
       </setting>
       <!-- Hades: ... and RGB at 12 bits first where it fits, on GeForce GTX 16 and RTX 20 (driver 620):
-- 
